# windom-1.21.3.zip = WinDom 1.21.3 (November 2004, Dominique Bereziat &
#   Arnaud Bercegeay), downloaded unchanged on 2026-10-06 from
#   https://downloads.sourceforge.net/project/windom/windom/1.21.3/windom-1.21.3.zip
#   SourceForge publishes SHA-1 77e31fa7264857c52d114fd06e79217dd90fda8f and
#   MD5 bf5088fbe0a58cd9969474b6a441a59b for it; both match. Its 397 files are
#   byte-identical to Applications/windom-1.21.3 (diff -r, 2026-10-06).
#
# patches/zview-windom-1.21.3.patch = the patch zView's build instructions
#   require ("Download & compile & install windom 1.21.3 after applying the
#   patch", zview/howto_build/howto.txt step 2), copied unchanged from
#   https://github.com/mikrosk/z-tools  zview/howto_build/windom-1.21.3.patch
#   (last changed in commit a556a6887fc031bfa30decfddd52023c8e703b75,
#   2011-10-22; checkout at 04805b77d6fc246ee507c8c5e2317b58b1a531e4 in
#   Applications/z-tools). 134 lines: ApplWrite/ApplSet read their variadic
#   WORDs as int (gcc4 va_arg promotion), av_ping copies the AV name into
#   app.pipe, and three cast-as-lvalue lines that gcc4 rejects.
